Step 1: Check CPU usage

top

or

htop

If any process is using very high CPU, I will identify it.

Step 2: Check Memory Usage

free -h

If RAM is full and swap usage is high, it may cause slowness.

Step 3: Check Disk Space

df -h

If a filesystem is 100% full, applications may stop working.

Step 4: Check Running Processes

ps -ef

Find processes consuming excessive CPU or memory.

Step 5: Check System Logs

Ubuntu

tail -50 /var/log/syslog.

RHEL

tail -50 /var/log/messages

Look for errors or warnings.
